An opportune time to mention the real-world example of when the authorities really wanted to gain full access to a computer but did not want to resort to legal compulsion or &quot;rubber-hose cryptanalysis&quot; -- they simply waited until the target was logged in, staged an altercation in the immediate vicinity, and then snatched the open laptop away from them.<p>You can read about the sting, here: 
&quot;How Did Investigators Catch the Dread Pirate Roberts (DPR) in San Francisco?&quot;
<a href="https://www.forensicscolleges.com/blog/forensics-casefile/silk-road" rel="nofollow">https://www.forensicscolleges.com/blog/forensics-casefile/si...</a>

