A stray &quot;J&quot; I encountered years ago: a certain client's support tickets would often end with a single &quot;J&quot;, which was a little confusing as it was not one of their name initials. After a brief investigation, the original email source contained this:<p><pre><code>    &lt;font face=&quot;<em>Wingdin</em>gs&quot;&gt;J&lt;/font&gt;
</code></pre>
Which renders as a smiley face.

